  "interpretation": [
    "The tested profile failed both the six-second first-link deadline and continuous-link requirement.",
    "At the sampled Linux handoff points, the expected native MCU version was still not reported. This rejects this tested profile as a solution; it does not show that the vendor driver never bound or that every possible UEFI implementation must fail.",
    "MCU transport completion does not establish RAM integrity or full firmware/calibration state.",
    "The diagnostic driver adds register reads and logs and preserves the normal native initialization decisions. This one diagnostic boot is not an unmodified performance distribution.",
    "SNP binding and ExitBootServices can call UNDI shutdown/stop; vendor source is unavailable, so the test does not isolate which firmware action accounts for the delay.",
    "The original firmware and driver are the rollback baseline; no production image recipe enables this experiment.",
    "The measured cached builder image and Python packages are recorded. The referenced wrapper uses Ubuntu package repositories and Python requirements that can resolve differently later, so a fresh build is not guaranteed byte-identical."
  ]
